+    Groups are sorted by their key in ascending order. Pass
+    ``reverse=True`` to sort them in descending order instead, such as
+    to show the newest or highest values first.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        <ul>{% for year, items in posts|groupby("year", reverse=True) %}
+          <li>{{ year }}: {{ items|length }} posts</li>
+        {% endfor %}</ul>
+
+    ``key_transform`` is a callable that formats the key of each group
+    for display. It is applied to the ``grouper`` of each group after
+    the items have been grouped and sorted, so it changes only the key
+    that is yielded, never which items end up together or the order of
+    the groups.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        <ul>{% for month, items in posts|groupby("date", key_transform=month_label) %}
+          <li>{{ month }}: {{ items|length }} posts</li>
+        {% endfor %}</ul>
+
+    .. versionchanged:: 3.1
+        Added the ``reverse`` and ``key_transform`` parameters.
+
     .. versionchanged:: 3.0
         Added the ``default`` parameter.
 
